      "side": 1,
      "message": "I got a bit confused about the part discussing stages for `TrackUsageAndGetResourceBarrier`.\n\nIn any case I believe that we should be able to completely remove the barrier call here, and instead in FinalizeMapImpl, have an ASSERT that `TrackUsageAndGetResourceBarrier` returns the null barrier.\n\nThat\u0027s because if the buffer is mappable and used in any submit, we know that it will be transitionend back to the mappable usage by `TransitionMappableBuffersEagerly`, which is always called before FinalizeMap runs (since the submit that contains the barriers generated by `TransitionMappableBuffersEagerly` is finished executing, so it is finished encoding).\n\nThe only other case would be for buffers that are map read + write if we mapped them with one usage and then the other, but even then the barrier should be empty AFAIU.",
